<h1 class="page-title">404</h1>
<p class="lede">
  There is no page at <code><nxl expr="path" /></code>.
</p>

<section class="panel">
  <p>
    This page is what the server returns for any path it does not recognise, and
    it is returned with a real <code>404</code> status — not a styled
    <code>200</code>, which would be worse for everyone, search engines included.
    The path above is the one you asked for, escaped like every other value.
  </p>
  <ul class="list">
    <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
    <li><a href="/about">About</a></li>
    <li><a href="/search">Search</a></li>
    <li><a href="/contact">Contact</a></li>
  </ul>
</section>
